\DOC BIGNUM_RANGE_TAC

\TYPE {BIGNUM_RANGE_TAC : string -> string -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Adds to the assumptions a size bound stating that a named bignum value is less
than {2 EXP (64 * k)} for a named length variable, leaving the conclusion
unchanged.

\DESCRIBE
The two arguments are strings naming variables occurring in the goal: {k} names
the length variable (the digit count) and {m} names the numeric value variable
to be bounded. The new assumption is appended at the end of the assumption
list; no existing assumption is removed or altered.
{
               A ?- t
   ===================================  BIGNUM_RANGE_TAC k m
     A, m < 2 EXP (64 * k) ?- t
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces the goals are {ensures}-style machine specifications
whose preconditions contain a {bignum_from_memory} equation tying the named
value to a block of the named length, and only this single kind of outcome
appears.

\ENDDOC
